					(name "Description") "Three plated holes, 1x3 on 2.54 mm   NOT a fitted header, which is why it is no longer called one. The footprint is an ordinary 1x3 header pattern and a strip could be soldered in for bring-up, but nothing is populated: a 1x3 body clears the Pmod shroud beside it by 0.09 mm, inside anyone's assembly tolerance. Drawn dashed with open holes so the sheet stops reading as a connector, the way the 2x3 it replaced did.")
			)
